🐍 1. Basic Password Reset Request Script

This script sends a password reset request to the application using the attacker’s username. It simulates the first step 
of the password recovery process where the server generates a reset token. The script uses the requests library to send an
HTTP POST request to the /forgot-password endpoint. The username parameter is included in the request body so the server
processes the reset request. Running this script allows testers to automate the initial password reset request instead of
manually submitting it through the browser. This can be useful when repeatedly testing the workflow during vulnerability
research. The script prints the response status code and message returned by the server so the tester can verify whether
the request was successful. It is a simple automation step that helps security researchers observe how the application 
behaves during the reset process. Such scripts are commonly used in penetration testing to quickly repeat actions and 
collect responses for analysis.


