🐍 3. Victim Password Reset Exploit Script

This script modifies the username parameter to target the victim account instead of the attacker’s account. Because the
application fails to validate the token, the attacker can change another user’s password by simply changing the username
field. The script sends a crafted POST request where the username is set to carlos and the token parameter is empty. If the
vulnerability exists, the server will reset the victim’s password to the value provided in the request. The script
demonstrates how attackers can automate account takeover attacks using simple HTTP requests. Security researchers can use
such scripts in a lab environment to demonstrate the real impact of broken password reset logic.

